  "notes": "Entirely business-type hospital; GAAP statements. Beginning net position 11,500,709 is 'beginning of year as restated' (printed beginning line shows '-' for 2025). Receipts: operating revenues by line (provision for bad debts is a negative line) plus nonoperating revenues; interest expense treated as disbursement. Schedule 1 Net Patient Service Revenue (p6) is entered in detail as the Total column lines (gross charges 48,822,392) with deductions (charity care 129,222, Medicare and Medicaid 5,476,952, commercial insurance and other 3,280,500) as negative lines; 48,822,392 - 129,222 - 8,757,452 = 39,935,718 ties to p3 and to the detail total. It repeats receipts[0] in detail only (detail is separate from receipts). Printed gross subtotal not entered as an item. Schedule 2 (p7-8) combined column 'Combined' 34,336,650 excludes depreciation 3,386,716; statement operating expenses 37,723,366 = 34,336,650 + 3,386,716 (p3). Schedule 2 'Supplies and Other' column mixes supplies, purchased services and benefits (benefits are in the Supplies and Other column: 13,838,592 + 4,436,329 = 18,274,921); recorded as supplies and materials (insurance line as insurance). Zero (dash) lines omitted. Balance sheet is the hospital's Statements of Financial Position; capital assets shown as gross less accumulated depreciation as printed. Schedule 3 operating statistics (p9) not financial. v7 re-trim added p5 (original p10, Statements of Cash Flows continued: reconciliation of operating income to net cash provided by operating activities, 3,571,905, and supplemental disclosure); it adds no new data. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
